&Q000541 = Letter from Aradŋu to Šulgi about irrigation work
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.3.1.03
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.3.1.03&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. lugal-ŋu₁₀-ra u₃-na-a-dug₄
#lem: lugal[king]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: Say to my lord: thus says @wPN{Aradŋu}, your servant: 
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. {m}arad-ŋu₁₀ arad-zu na-ab-be₂-a
#lem: Aradŋu[1]PN; arad[slave]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. lugal-ŋu₁₀ niŋ₂ na-me-še₃ a₂-še mu-e-da-a-aŋ₂
#lem: lugal[king]; niŋ[thing]; name[any]; aše[now]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: My lord, 
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. a-ab-ba kur dilmun{ki}-na-ta
#lem: aʾabak[sea]; kur[mountain(s)]; Dilmun[1]GN
#tr.en: you have given me instructions about every matter, 
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. (1:a mun₄ gaba kur mar-tu{ki}-ta:1)
#lem: a[water]; mun[salt]; gaba[breast]; kur[mountain(s)]; Martu[1 Amorite]
#tr.en: from the sea and the land of @wGN{Dilmun}, 
#etcsl: line-id=5

:5v.1.1: ($some mss. have instead:$) a mun₄ gaba kur mar-tu{ki}-še₃
#lem: a[water]; mun[salt]; gaba[breast]; kur[mountain(s)]; Martu[1 Amorite]

6. (1:da#:1) si-mu-ur-ru-um (2:[ma]-da X{ki}-še₃:2)
#lem: dag[side]; Simurrum[1]SN; mada[land]; X[1]SN
#tr.en: @varh[t3103.v1]{from the salt waters and the borders of the land of the @wEN{Martu} } @vart[t3103.v2,t3103.v1]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} to the salt waters and the borders of the land of the @wEN{Martu} }, @varh[t3103.v3]{to } @vart[t3103.v4,t3103.v3]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} from } the @varh[t3103.v5]{side (?) } @vart[t3103.v6,t3103.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} borders (?) } of @wSN{Simurrum} and @varh[t3103.v7]{the territory of …… } @vart[t3103.v8,t3103.v7]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} the territory of @wGN{Subir} }: 
#etcsl: line-id=6

:6v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) gaba#
#lem: gaba[breast]
:6v.2.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) ma-da su-bir₄{ki}-ta
#lem: mada[land]; Subir[1]GN

7. iri{ki} dili-dili-bi (1:ma-da-ma-da-bi:1)
#lem: iri[city]; dili[single]; mada[land]
#tr.en: Their various cities and @varh[t3103.v9]{all their environs } @vart[t3103.v10,t3103.v9]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} their troops }, their canals, 
#etcsl: line-id=7

:7v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) ugnim-be₂-ne
#lem: ugnim[army]

8. id₂ a-šag₄ a-gar₃-bi u₃ eg₂ pa₅-bi
#lem: id[river]; ašag[field]; agar[meadow]; u[and]; eg[levee]; par[(small) canal]
#tr.en: fields, arable tracts and their embankments and ditches, 
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. igi X IN X X DU en šag₄ X X
#lem: igi[eye]; X; X; X; X; X; en[lord]; šag[heart]; X; X
#tr.en: All the cities are listening to my lord. 
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. iri{ki}-iri{ki} ŋiš tuku lugal-ŋu₁₀
#lem: iri[city]; ŋeš[tree]; tuku[acquire]; lugal[king]
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. ki X X X BI X X X ur₂ X X X X
#lem: ki[place]; X; X; X; X; X; X; X; ur[loin]; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. bad₃-bi en-nu-uŋ₃ kalag-ga bi₂-gub
#lem: bad[wall]; ennuŋ[watch]; kalag[strong]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: I have established strong guards for their fortresses, 
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. ugnim-bi gu₂ ŋiš bi₂-ŋar-ŋar
#lem: ugnim[army]; gu[neck]; ŋeš[tree]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: and I have made all their troops submit. 
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. X sig X X X X NE X X
#lem: X; sig[weak]; X; X; X; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. a-gar₃ a ŋar-ra-bi a-ta im-ta-e₃
#lem: agar[meadow]; a[water]; ŋar[put]; a[water]; e[leave]
#tr.en: I have drained the arable tracts when they were flooded. 
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. X eg₂ zal-la-bi X bi₂-ak
#lem: X; eg[levee]; zal[pass time]; X; ak[do]
#tr.en: I have …… when their embankments were leaky (?). 
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. X X a-šag₄-bi ŋiš-gi X-ra
#lem: X; X; ašag[field]; ŋešgi[thicket]; X
#tr.en: I have …… their fields and reedbeds. 
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. [...] X-ke₄ saŋ sag₃-ge X-bi
#lem: X; X; saŋ[head]; sag[strike]; X
#tr.en: …… bowing their heads ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=18

$ (4 lines fragmentary)
$ (unknown no. of lines missing)






